---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const githubInstallUrl = "https://github.com/apps/striff-app/installations/new";
const apiBaseUrl = "https://api.striff.io";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Pricing | Striff"
  description="Free for public repositories. Paid plans for private-repo teams that want automated structural review inside GitHub."
  canonical="https://striff.io/pricing"
>
  <main class="bg-slate-50 text-slate-900">
    <section class="mx-auto flex max-w-6xl flex-col gap-8 px-6 py-16 md:py-24">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <p class="mb-4 inline-flex rounded-full border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 px-4 py-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-amber-800" data-reveal>
          Pricing
        </p>
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950 md:text-6xl" data-reveal>
          Free for public repos. Paid for private-team rollout.
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600" data-reveal>
          Start with public pull requests for free. Upgrade when your team wants automated structural review, shared GitHub checks, and private-repo coverage.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="pricing-overview" data-reveal>
        <div class="pricing-overview-card">
          <span class="pricing-overview-kicker">Best entry point</span>
          <p>Use the extension on public repositories first, then expand into shared team workflow.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pricing-overview-card">
          <span class="pricing-overview-kicker">Paid boundary</span>
          <p>Private repositories, centralized checks, billing, and broader rollout across a team.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-3">
        <article class="rounded-[2rem] border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm" data-reveal>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="icon-badge icon-badge-emerald" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="m8.5 12 2.2 2.2 4.8-4.8"/></svg>
            </span>
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-slate-500">Free</p>
          </div>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-black text-slate-950">$0</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">Public repositories</p>
          <ul class="feature-list mt-6 space-y-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-700">
            <li>Chrome extension for public PR review</li>
            <li>Structural diffs, unusual-edge signals, and grounded notes</li>
            <li>Good fit for open-source projects and evaluation</li>
            <li>Community support</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/striffs-for-github/gcbcjajnjbplgkhnbemlkadgnjnfjoen" class="btn-secondary mt-8 inline-flex" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Install</a>
        </article>

        <article class="rounded-[2rem] border border-blue-300 bg-gradient-to-b from-blue-600 to-slate-950 p-8 text-white shadow-xl" data-reveal>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="icon-badge icon-badge-dark-blue" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"><path d="M16 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H7a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9.5" cy="7" r="3"/><path d="M20 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"/><path d="M16 4.13a3 3 0 0 1 0 5.74"/></svg>
            </span>
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-blue-100">Team</p>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-3 flex items-end gap-2">
            <h2 class="text-4xl font-black">$10</h2>
            <p class="pb-1 text-sm text-blue-100">per seat / month</p>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-blue-100">Private repositories and shared team workflow</p>
          <ul class="feature-list feature-list-light mt-6 space-y-3 text-sm leading-6 text-blue-50">
            <li>Everything in Free</li>
            <li>GitHub App posts structural review output on private PRs</li>
            <li>Centralized checks instead of one-user extension-only review</li>
            <li>Billing and account management tied to your installation</li>
            <li>Email support</li>
          </ul>
          <button id="pro-checkout-button" class="btn-primary mt-8 inline-flex bg-white text-slate-950 hover:bg-blue-50">
            Start plan
          </button>
          <p id="checkout-status" class="mt-4 text-sm text-blue-100"></p>
        </article>

        <article class="rounded-[2rem] border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm" data-reveal>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="icon-badge icon-badge-amber" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"><path d="M12 2v20"/><path d="M17 5H9.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 0 0 7H14.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 7H6"/></svg>
            </span>
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-slate-500">Enterprise</p>
          </div>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-black text-slate-950">Custom</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">For internal platforms and compliance-heavy teams</p>
          <ul class="feature-list mt-6 space-y-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-700">
            <li>Private deployment and internal-network constraints</li>
            <li>SSO and audit-oriented workflows</li>
            <li>Priority analysis and higher volume</li>
            <li>Private deployment options</li>
            <li>Dedicated support</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="/contact" class="btn-secondary mt-8 inline-flex">Talk to us</a>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-[2rem] border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm" data-reveal>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-950">How the upgrade path works</h2>
        <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600 md:grid-cols-3">
          <p><strong class="text-slate-900">1.</strong> Prove Striff on public pull requests first. The extension is free and that is the intended entry point.</p>
          <p><strong class="text-slate-900">2.</strong> Install the GitHub App when your team wants structural review on private repositories.</p>
          <p><strong class="text-slate-900">3.</strong> Stripe Checkout attaches billing to a specific installation and the customer portal handles invoices and cancellation.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script is:inline define:vars={{ apiBaseUrl, githubInstallUrl }}>
    const params = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);
    const installationId = params.get("installation_id");
    const button = document.getElementById("pro-checkout-button");
    const status = document.getElementById("checkout-status");

    if (button && !installationId) {
      status.textContent = "Install the GitHub App first so billing can be attached to a specific installation.";
      button.addEventListener("click", () => {
        window.location.href = githubInstallUrl;
      });
    }

    if (button && installationId) {
      status.textContent = `Preparing checkout for installation ${installationId}.`;
      button.addEventListener("click", async () => {
        status.textContent = "Creating Stripe Checkout session...";
        try {
          const response = await fetch(`${apiBaseUrl}/api/v1/billing/checkout?installation_id=${encodeURIComponent(installationId)}`, {
            method: "POST"
          });
          if (!response.ok) {
            throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);
          }
          const payload = await response.json();
          if (payload.checkoutUrl) {
            window.location.href = payload.checkoutUrl;
            return;
          }
          throw new Error("Missing checkoutUrl");
        } catch (error) {
          status.textContent = "Could not start checkout yet. Verify the backend deployment and installation ID.";
        }
      });
    }
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
